"""
Order Get It Right -- Inventory Agent (v1.0.0)

Walks local drive paths the operator names, classifies every file into a
single category, and seals a deterministic inventory report to the Merkle
truth ledger. The agent is the answer to the operator question:

  "What is on my drives that is project material? What is library noise?
   What is duplicated? What did the previous session leave behind that
   I never knew about?"

Same shape as the other agents: a class with a method, sealed to the
chain. No LLM. No network. No external dependencies. The walk is
read-only -- the agent never modifies, moves, or deletes a file. The
first 200 bytes of each file are read for content sniffing; the rest
is left alone. Credential-shaped files are redacted by name only; their
contents are never read into memory or written to the chain.

Classification (exactly one tag per file):

  PROJECT_CODE      -- source code inside the OrderGetItRight build tree
                       (02_Technical/**/*.py, 02_Technical/**/*.html, etc.)
  PROJECT_DOC       -- human-readable project documents under 00_Strategy,
                       01_Methodology, the validation folder (md/txt)
  BUILD_ARTEFACT    -- generated / cache files inside the build
                       (__pycache__, .pytest_cache, .bak-pre-* backups)
  PROJECT_INPUT     -- input samples and research files the operator
                       fed in (data/samples/*, to the spoils go, gemini
                       to evalue)
  LIBRARY_NOISE     -- Python files that look like stdlib / third-party
                       library code (virtualenv, pytest, pip, etc.) and
                       are clearly not part of this build
  PERSONAL          -- anything under the operator's home that is not
                       part of the project (photos, music, browser data)
  DUPLICATE         -- a file whose SHA-256 has already been inventoried
                       in this run
  REDACTED_LOCATION -- a file whose name suggests credentials or secrets;
                       its path and size are recorded, its contents and
                       SHA-256 are NOT
  UNKNOWN           -- a file that did not match any rule; logged so the
                       operator can add a new rule if it matters

Determinism. Two consecutive runs on the same machine, against the same
paths, with the same operator, produce byte-identical reports unless a
file was added, removed, or modified between runs. The mtime is
captured in the report so a future operator can tell which inventory
captured which state of the disk.

Boundary. The agent lives in 02_Technical/src/agents/. It imports
from stdlib and from src.io.vault_io only. It does NOT import from
src/agents/orchestrator or from any other agent; it is a leaf node.
Tests/ cannot import from this module (the boundary test enforces
that); the agent is invoked via its CLI entry point.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

